          "targetDoi": "10.1016/0378-4371(92)90283-v",
          "snippet": "The master equation is an ordinary differential equation when the state space is discrete and becomes an integral-differential equation in the case of continuous states. It has been widely used in various stochastic processes, including random walks, birth-death processes, general chemical reaction systems, 17,18 thermal unimolecular reactions at low pressures, 19 single-molecule enzyme kinetics in open biochemical systems 20 etc.",
